\title{KZG and the Pairing-Based Line}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Constant-size proofs and a constant-time verifier, at the price of a trusted setup and a pairing-friendly curve. Still the endpoint of most [wrapping](dhsorens-003P) pipelines because the on-chain verifier is cheap.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The scheme and its security assumption; what the structured reference string contains.}
        \li{The pairing check, and why the verifier is constant-time regardless of degree.}
        \li{Batching and multi-point openings.}
        \li{Trusted setup in practice: ceremonies, updatability, and what a compromised setup permits.}
        \li{Why it does not scale to zkVM-sized traces, and where it survives anyway.}
    }
}
